CORE
main.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ x: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ the threads may have set x: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Closures (code and environment pointers) on the heap, created after the first
spawn and published to a thread. The value sets of their fields must not keep
the initial (nondeterministic) values or the values of other objects: calls
through them would otherwise consider every function of the type, which
recurses without bound.
